# Implementation Plan - Development Password Reset Link

To address the lack of an SMTP mail server in the local development/demo environment, we will return the generated reset token link in the response of the forgot password request and render a secure reset link directly on the success screen of the frontend.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [api/v1/endpoints/auth.py](file:///c:/Users/admin/Desktop/HumanResources_New/HumanResources/HumanResources/backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/auth.py)
- Update `forgot_password` route to capture the return `token` of `AuthService.request_password_reset`.
- Include the `reset_link` value (`/reset-password/{token}`) in the response body.

---

### Frontend

#### [MODIFY] [api/resumeiq.ts](file:///c:/Users/admin/Desktop/HumanResources_New/HumanResources/HumanResources/frontend/src/api/resumeiq.ts)
- Update `forgotPassword` API helper signature to accept `{ message: string; reset_link?: string }` response.

#### [MODIFY] [pages/ForgotPassword.tsx](file:///c:/Users/admin/Desktop/HumanResources_New/HumanResources/HumanResources/frontend/src/pages/ForgotPassword.tsx)
- Keep track of `resetLink` using a React state variable.
- Capture the returned `reset_link` in `handleSubmit` and set it in state.
- Render a helpful direct link section on the success screen, informing the user that they can click it to reset the password directly (simulating the email receipt for local testing).

